# Topic ACLs. The `user` names must match the credentials created by entrypoint.sh.
#
# Backend: owns ingestion and alert publishing, so it needs read/write on the whole systems/# tree.
# Dashboards: read-only, and only the two topics the UI actually consumes. A dashboard credential
# can never publish, which means a compromised browser session cannot forge an alarm.

user backend
topic readwrite systems/#

user dashboard
topic read systems/+/alarm
topic read systems/+/events

# The ESP32 terminals use the dashboard credentials in the reference deployment. If you give each
# terminal its own account, add a `user <name>` block with the same two read rules.
